# DSH Service Blueprint Living SSoT Guard

For any DSH-related work, first read and respect:

packages/surfaces/src/service-owned/dsh/SERVICE_BLUEPRINT.md

## Mandatory Rules

1. SERVICE_BLUEPRINT.md is the canonical living control file for DSH.
2. Never recreate docs/services/dsh.
3. Never use packages/surfaces/src/dsh/... as a live path.
4. Never paste noisy generated screen catalogs into the blueprint.
5. Never mark Binding, Integration, API, Runtime Vars, Guards, QA, or full DSH closure as VERIFIED/CLOSED unless SERVICE_BLUEPRINT.md is updated with evidence.
6. Any DSH closure script must update or verify SERVICE_BLUEPRINT.md.
7. Any DSH evidence must be written under kdt/volatile/registry/runs/{SESSION_ID}.
8. DSH order flows must use order/orders, not task/tasks.

